mission "A Bargain with Black Jack"
    name "A Bargain with Black Jack"
    description "Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
    source "Port Azure"
    destination "Gallows Key"
    reward 1655
    speaker offer "Black Jack Rourke"
    speaker visit "Black Jack Rourke"
    speaker complete "Black Jack Rourke"
    to offer
        has "The Fleet at the Blue Line: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals.`
            `Black Jack Rourke studies you for a moment. "The old sea charter settled one war, but it did not settle the past. The lost expedition sailed west under a sealed order, and its wake is stirring every ambitious captain in these waters."
            choice
                `(I will help uncover what happened.)`
                    accept
                `(Tell me what you are not saying.)`
                    goto details
                `(I have no wish to be drawn into another quarrel.)`
                    close
            label details
                `Black Jack Rourke lowers their voice. "The maps were altered, the convoy erased from the books, and someone has been buying witnesses. Follow the evidence, not the flags."`
                choice
                    `(Then I will take the matter in hand.)`
                        accept
                    `(Not today.)`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Bargain with Black Jack. Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Black Jack Rourke receives you at Gallows Key. The evidence fits another piece into the puzzle: the expedition was not searching for gold alone, but for a place deliberately removed from every official chart.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Black Jack Rourke thanks you. "Every answer makes the sea less simple, captain. Yet the truth belongs to the people who live here, not to the first crown or company that can put a seal upon it."`
        log "Completed A Bargain with Black Jack. Received 1655 gold. Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
